GIMP Palette
Name: Roguelike — Ash Catacombs
Columns: 6
#
# Direction: cold stone, no daylight, one torch. The darkest palette in the
# repo and the least colourful on purpose.
#
# crypt-* is six steps of blue-grey and carries almost the whole screen. Six
# steps of near-nothing sounds like waste until you remember this game draws a
# 60x34 tile dungeon: at that density, value *is* the level geometry — floor,
# wall, wall-face, rubble and dark are all the same colour at different
# brightnesses, and a hue would only get in the way.
#
# torch-* is the only warmth and it is rationed. Whatever is lit is either the
# player's light or something that wants to eat them, which makes "warm" a
# gameplay signal rather than a mood. blood-mark is smaller still — a hit
# marker and nothing else.
#
# bile-* gives the monsters a hue the architecture never uses, so a moving
# thing separates from a static thing before the player has parsed either.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 18  20  26	crypt-0-pit
 32  36  46	crypt-1
 52  58  72	crypt-2
 78  86 102	crypt-3
112 122 142	crypt-4
160 170 190	crypt-5-hilite
 38  54  46	bile-0-shadow
 66  96  74	bile-1
104 142 106	bile-2
152 192 150	bile-3-hilite
150  70  26	torch-0-shadow
214 124  36	torch-1
248 178  74	torch-2
